# Command line options for the rpki-prover systemd service.
#
# rpki-prover has no configuration file; everything is a command line option.
# "rpki-prover --help" lists all of them, and rpki-prover(1) has the same list.
#
# --rpki-root-directory /var/lib/rpki-prover is always passed by the unit file
# and must not be repeated here.
#
# The value is split on whitespace by systemd, so options containing spaces
# cannot be expressed here; use a systemd drop-in
# (systemctl edit rpki-prover) for those.

RPKI_PROVER_ARGS="--cpu-count 2 --http-api-port 9999"

# Trust anchor locators
# ---------------------
# On the first start, when /var/lib/rpki-prover/tals is empty and
# --extra-tals-directory is not set, rpki-prover downloads the five RIR TALs
# from the RIRs themselves. That is the default and needs no configuration.
#
# To use the TALs from the Debian archive instead, install the
# rpki-trust-anchors package and add
#
#   --extra-tals-directory /etc/tals
#
# to RPKI_PROVER_ARGS above. Setting it also switches off the automatic
# download, so make sure the directory really has the TALs you want. Note that
# Debian 12 (bookworm) ships rpki-trust-anchors without the ARIN TAL.
#
# Locally added or replacement TALs can always be dropped into
# /var/lib/rpki-prover/tals/ , which is scanned on every start.

# Some other things you may want in RPKI_PROVER_ARGS:
#
#   --log-level debug
#   --with-rtr --rtr-address 0.0.0.0 --rtr-port 8283
#   --revalidation-interval 600
#   --cache-lifetime-hours 48
#   --local-exceptions /etc/rpki-prover/slurm.json
